Strengthened institutional arrangements and working processes for official food safety controls, consistent with the risk analysis framework;
Improved knowledge and practical skills in food safety risk communication, and response capacities for food safety emergencies;
Increased capacities of national food safety authorities to implement risk-based inspection and improve their collaboration with food business operators on food safety risk management.
Output 4. Increased capacities of food business operators and the public authorities on food safety management practices to reduce food safety risks in selected value chains.

Regional workshops on planning and policy development for increased aquaculture production;
Regional Training on strengthening of the organizational capacity of fish farmers associations and SMEs in processing, marketing and trade of fish products through engagement at community level;
Preparation/adaptation of Best Management Practices (BMPs) for aquaculture farm management;
Regional workshop on freshwater fish hatchery management of main species for improved food security and human nutrition.

Sustainable field surveillance system to detect trans boundary animal diseases (TADs) on a timely manner is established and enhanced;
Steps toward World Organization for Animal Health (OIE) freedom status from PPR are made;
Diagnostic capacity of central and regional laboratories for selected TADs is improved;

Awareness raising of the values of ecosystem goods and service benefits derived from pollinators (local and national level);
Forest surveyor methodologies for inclusion of pollinators in forest management planning;
Participatory management planning of forest management plans;
Management practices for promoting ‘bee plants’ and the conservation management for wild pollinators beyond managed honey bees; etc.

This output is within "Project Preparation and Visibility Activities for FAO Azerbaijan Partnership Program. Output includes:
Preparation and design of the Gender Sensitive Visibility Strategy and Plan;
Production of information and advocacy material, including caps, T-shirts, posters, brochure, fact sheets, calendar;
Development of a dedicated FAPP web site;
Provide timely information to relevant media on FAPP projects activities. Composition and dissemination of news-releases. Visibility materials also to focus onto socio–economic development in rural areas, especially for women and youth.

A methodological mechanism for data collection, assessment and reporting developed;
An Operational National Forest Assessment and Monitoring System established;
Improved forest management planning in 2 pilot areas;
Income generating activities for local small farm holders demonstrated and the possibility for their application is investigated;
Carbon stocks enhanced in degraded and deforested forest fund land;
Sustainability and upscale Sustainable Forest Management ensured through provision of up to date information on forest resources and their trend and dissemination of lessons learned and good practices.
